 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 21,
   "y": 3,
   "text": "CAMERA OBSCURA. Claims to be the world's biggest. Shows the whole bay on a table. Today the table shows drizzle."
  },
  {
   "x": 20,
   "y": 12,
   "text": "CLIFF RAILWAY. 1896. Up in 4 minutes, down in 4 minutes, a lifetime of 'one more go' in between."
  },
  {
   "x": 11,
   "y": 11,
   "text": "CONSTITUTION HILL, 130 m. The 'Constitution' is a walk. Not a law."
  },
  {
   "x": 36,
   "y": 17,
   "text": "ABERYSTWYTH UNIVERSITY. Founded 1872 on pennies from ordinary Welsh people. First college of its kind in Wales. Don't leave bikes on the grass."
  },
  {
   "x": 45,
   "y": 18,
   "text": "NATIONAL LIBRARY OF WALES. Quiet please. The Black Book of Carmarthen is asleep."
  },
  {
   "x": 21,
   "y": 35,
   "text": "ABERYSTWYTH CASTLE. Edward I, 1277. Blown up after the Civil War. A very old ruin with a very good sea view."
  },
  {
   "x": 33,
   "y": 36,
   "text": "ABERYSTWYTH HARBOUR. Tide times on the board. The board is optimistic."
  }
 ],
